# Weight profile nemotron-super-vl-nvfp4: NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Super VL 120B-A12B in NVIDIA's own ModelOpt checkpoint
# (nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-NVFP4 at revision 8a115b9d, 75.1 GB): routed and shared experts
# NVFP4 (group 16), the Mamba2 and attention projections and the head FP8 with a tensor scale, read as stored
# (activations bf16, KV cache bf16; the vision tower not loaded). Text only. Measured 2026-10-16 against BF16 (8 wikitext
# rows x 1,024): KL 0.041, top-1 93.4 %, perplexity 3.834 (BF16 3.840); decode 19.6 tok/s; with LiLiCorr and the lookup
# 23.8 / 28.4 / 39.9 / 73.4 / 80.1 tok/s on prose / chat / code / edit / copy asks, every text the plain run's.
# Switch with ops/use-profile.sh nemotron-super-vl-nvfp4.
QSE_NH_MODEL=nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b
QSE_NH_VARIANT=super-vl-nvfp4
QSE_NH_DIR=${HOME}/models/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b-nvfp4
QSE_WEIGHTS_GB=75.1
MAX_LEN=131072
# MemAvailable (GiB) a start needs: the weights (66.63 allocated, measured), the engine and its graphs, the allocator,
# the prefill workspace, three slots' KV and LiLiCorr's rings, LiLiCorr and the 15 GiB floor
QSE_MEM_NEED_GIB=95
# the engine's limits: 77.5 GiB taken from MemAvailable with LiLiCorr and 3 slots at 140,000 tokens (measured)
MEM_CEILING_GIB=78
MEM_PEAK_GIB=84
# NVIDIA's LiLiCorr drafter for Super VL: a draft head of the tree drafter beside the lookup
QSE_NH_HEAD=lilicorr
QSE_NH_LILICORR=${HOME}/models/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-lilicorr
. "${REPO}/ops/profiles/_nemotron.env"
QSE_WEIGHTS_HF=nvidia/NVIDIA-Nemotron-3.5-Super-VL-120B-A12B-NVFP4
QSE_WEIGHTS_REVISION=8a115b9d966adce8c059a7bcf47f49a1e57957d8
QSE_ASSETS="${QSE_NH_LILICORR}/model.safetensors"
